==English==
[[Image:Flag of Edward England.svg|thumb|The flag of [[w:Edward England|Edward England]], a well-known symbol of piracy]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|pyracy||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|ML.|pīrātia}}, from Classical {{der|en|la|pīrāta}} + {{m|la|ia}}, or {{der|en|grc|πειρατεία}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpaɪɹəsi/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-piracy.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|nautical}} [[robbery|Robbery]] at [[sea]], a violation of international law; taking a [[ship]] away from the control of those who are legally entitled to it.
#: {{syn|en|pirateship}}
#: {{ux|en|How should the international community respond to Somali '''piracy'''?}}
# A similar violation of international law, such as [[hijacking]] of an [[aircraft]].
# The [[unauthorized]] [[duplication]] of [[goods]] protected by [[intellectual property]] [[law]].
#: {{ux|en|Some video game consoles use specially designed cartridges to make software '''piracy''' more difficult.}}
# The [[operation]] of an [[unlicensed]] [[radio]] or [[television]] [[station]].
# {{lb|en|ornithology}} [[kleptoparasitism|Kleptoparasitism]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|robbery at sea}} {{l|en|buccaneerism}}
* {{sense|breaking intellectual property law by making unauthorized copies}} {{l|en|bootlegging}}, {{l|en|file sharing}}

====Hyponyms====
* {{l|en|air piracy}}

